A||||18||Spektrum-87GT||is it even possible to flip the fiero in a turn?||||1||
Z||000000||Spektrum-87GT||10-05-2001||06:33 PM||||ok, im talking about speeds less than 60mph, it seems i can take turns VERY fast, but that goes without saying because its mid-engined... anyway, has anyone ever flipped their fiero? is it possible?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Leper||10-05-2001||06:42 PM||||Anything's possible. The most likely way it's going to happen is if the car "trips" on a curb or something or if it gets airborne.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||10-05-2001||06:45 PM||||I'd say the most immediate concern is losing traction and spinning out, which could lead to flipping if it hits something, or goes into a ditch, etc..<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Master_Sushi||10-05-2001||07:18 PM||||I don't think its possable to flip a fiero, unless hiting something or jumping it and going airborn. I span my old 88 coupe and my 84 a few times. I never worried about them tiping over, more so worrying about hiting things while it happens. I never span at over 50mph, in my fieros anyway  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.<P>Basicly if you flip a fiero... YOU did something very wrong.||||reg||10
